course: dictionary
lesson: 3778
title: Food and food for thought
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Food is what people, animals and plants take in to stay alive, grow and have energy. «Pizza is my favourite food.» Here food means a particular kind of thing to eat. Food is usually uncountable, so we say some food, not a food.
explain: Food can also mean an idea. «Food for thought» means something worth thinking about for a while. When your teacher says, «That question is food for thought,» she is not talking about lunch.
explain: Other words mean food too, but they feel different. Grub, nosh and chow are casual, like a chat with friends. Provisions and sustenance are stiff, formal words you might find in a book or on a notice. Pick the word that fits the kind of talk you are in.
fact: Food is what people, animals and plants take in to stay alive, grow and have energy.
fact: «Food» can be a particular kind of thing to eat, such as «pizza is my favourite food».
fact: «Food for thought» means something worth thinking about.
fact: Casual words for food include «grub», «nosh» (UK), «tucker» (Australia), «chow» (US) and «scran» (UK).
fact: Formal words for food include «provisions», «sustenance», «nourishment» and «foodstuffs».
exercise: «Pizza is my favourite food.» In this sentence, food means | A kind of bird | Something worth thinking about | A bag for carrying shopping | *A particular kind of thing to eat
exercise: «The film's ending was food for thought.» What does food for thought mean? | *Something worth thinking about | A lunch you can take to school | Something you cook in a pan
exercise: Which word for food is formal? | Chow | Nosh | *Sustenance | Grub
test: «Gulls have learned that people carry food.» Here food means | Something worth thinking about | *Something people and animals eat | A shop that sells cakes
test: Which word for food is casual, like a chat with friends? | Provisions | Comestibles | Foodstuffs | *Scran
exam: Which sentence uses food correctly? | We ate a food at the picnic. | *We ate plenty of food at the picnic. | We ate many food at the picnic.
